WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.861
- I think I've came up
with the largest collection

00:00:03.861 --> 00:00:06.694
of old American cars in the world.

00:00:08.789 --> 00:00:11.206
Yeah, all of 'em has a story,

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.099
but they've kindly take their
place in the forest, you know,

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:18.766
and they are part of the forest.

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:23.992
They grew up partially in the forest.

00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:27.159
(inspirational music)

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:30.898
My name is Walter Dean Lewis.

00:00:30.898 --> 00:00:34.481
I run and operate and
own Old Car City USA.

00:00:36.048 --> 00:00:38.238
I was born and raised in a junk yard,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.071
and I like junk yards.

00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:46.618
This land was clear when I
started putting 'em in there.

00:00:46.618 --> 00:00:48.478
I wanted nature to take its course,

00:00:48.478 --> 00:00:50.728
and we just let it go wild.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.838
These cars come from other junk yards

00:00:54.838 --> 00:00:58.248
and just individual people,
and they all wind up

00:00:58.248 --> 00:00:59.998
here at Old Car City.

00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:06.738
Fords, Chevrolets, General Motors,

00:01:06.738 --> 00:01:10.821
they laying out there in
the forest rotting away.

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:17.258
We build things out of rust out there,

00:01:17.258 --> 00:01:19.608
and it is a piece of art.

00:01:19.608 --> 00:01:22.775
(inspirational music)

